# KEBU SINGLE-SLICE EXECUTION RULE

**Master contract:** `docs/product/KEBU-MASTER-ENGINEERING-INSTRUCTION.md` · `kebu-master-engineering.mdc`

Implement **only** the assigned vertical slice.

- Do not begin later slices.
- Do not placeholder future slices.
- Do not modify unrelated systems unless required.
- **If a dependency is broken:** **STOP** — repair it end-to-end before continuing. Do not build on broken functionality.

Workflow: inspect → report (exists/missing/files/DB/authz/flow/acceptance/tests/risks) → implement complete path → test → manual verify → adversarial audit → repair → completion report.

Complete path: user action → FE → validation → authenticated request → authz → business logic → **Supabase** → DB → response → UI → refresh persistence.

Forbidden: FE-only · unused APIs · fake success · **hidden/suppressed errors** · memory-only save · hard-coded prod data · tests that mock away the behavior under test · **new features on broken prior slices**.

Never say complete unless FE + BE + DB are connected and verified.
